<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- App-host Activity theme for the C++ MAUI gallery on Android.

     WHY THIS EXISTS (parity):
     The Activity previously declared NO android:theme. With targetSdkVersion 34 that makes the framework
     apply Theme.DeviceDefault (Material You / Material3) on API-34 devices, whose ?android:colorBackground
     resolves to the Material3 *tonal surface* — a very slightly purple-tinted white (measured #F1F0F7 on
     the maui-test emulator). Real .NET MAUI (MauiAppCompatActivity + Maui.MainTheme, whose base parent is
     Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight) renders these native-default ContentPages on a PURE WHITE window
     background (#FFFFFF) in light mode. That mismatch is what the parity review flagged as "port page
     background is light lavender-gray vs MAUI's white" (content_view, menu_bar, and every sparse page).

     THE FIX:
     Pin an explicit light theme and force the window / colorBackground to pure white so it matches MAUI's
     rendered background exactly, instead of inheriting the M3 tonal surface. We parent on the framework
     DeviceDefault.Light.DarkActionBar (no Material Components AAR on the app-host classpath — the app-host
     links android.jar only, no gradle) and KEEP the action bar: app_host.cpp's content_chrome_height_px
     measures the status-bar + action-bar height to lay the page out below the chrome, so removing the
     action bar would change every page's layout. The scoped change here is the background color only. -->
<resources>
    <style name="MauiAppHost.Theme" parent="@android:style/Theme.DeviceDefault.Light.DarkActionBar">
        <!-- Match MAUI's white light-mode page background (Theme.MaterialComponents.DayNight resolves to
             white), instead of the DeviceDefault/Material3 tonal surface (#F1F0F7 lavender). Both the
             window drawable and the colorBackground attribute are pinned so surfaces that read either one
             land on pure white. -->
        <item name="android:windowBackground">@android:color/white</item>
        <item name="android:colorBackground">@android:color/white</item>
    </style>
</resources>
